{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\_cls6_jpg\\drawing\\075.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Mounting and Framing", "conf": 0.866, "box": [[189, 73], [743, 44], [746, 93], [191, 122]]}, {"text": "drawings. Before framing we usually", "conf": 0.872, "box": [[171, 274], [840, 235], [843, 277], [173, 316]]}, {"text": "mount artworks.", "conf": 0.894, "box": [[168, 342], [443, 323], [446, 360], [170, 380]]}, {"text": "Step 1:", "conf": 0.779, "box": [[159, 448], [284, 441], [286, 490], [161, 497]]}, {"text": "This is a 6x8 inches pencil", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[291, 504], [871, 471], [874, 514], [293, 547]]}, {"text": "sketch. First of all, it is to be cut into an", "conf": 0.912, "box": [[157, 576], [871, 538], [873, 579], [159, 616]]}, {"text": "accurate rectangular shape. Next we", "conf": 0.923, "box": [[151, 641], [873, 605], [875, 647], [153, 683]]}, {"text": "will paste it on a harder sheet of paper", "conf": 0.924, "box": [[149, 701], [872, 671], [874, 718], [151, 748]]}, {"text": "which is larger than the drawing so that", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[145, 766], [874, 742], [876, 784], [146, 808]]}, {"text": "we get two to four inches border on all", "conf": 0.886, "box": [[138, 832], [874, 806], [876, 849], [139, 875]]}, {"text": "the four sides. You can also keep the", "conf": 0.897, "box": [[132, 894], [873, 873], [874, 920], [133, 940]]}, {"text": "lower margin a little larger than the", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[126, 961], [871, 942], [872, 985], [127, 1004]]}, {"text": "others.", "conf": 0.842, "box": [[120, 1025], [255, 1023], [256, 1068], [121, 1070]]}, {"text": "Fig: 5.1", "conf": 0.801, "box": [[1205, 1062], [1325, 1058], [1327, 1100], [1207, 1104]]}, {"text": "Step 2", "conf": 0.841, "box": [[116, 1130], [255, 1127], [256, 1179], [117, 1182]]}, {"text": "ingilab.com", "conf": 0.887, "box": [[762, 1195], [1055, 1024], [1085, 1075], [792, 1247]]}, {"text": "The colour of the hardpaper is also very important. For coloured", "conf": 0.922, "box": [[255, 1237], [1622, 1200], [1623, 1249], [257, 1286]]}, {"text": "paintings we choose a colour that is in harmony", "conf": 0.949, "box": [[653, 1295], [1624, 1264], [1625, 1320], [655, 1351]]}, {"text": "with the colour scheme of the painting. Here we", "conf": 0.952, "box": [[661, 1368], [1621, 1339], [1622, 1389], [663, 1418]]}, {"text": "will choose from tones of gray for the pencil", "conf": 0.913, "box": [[657, 1440], [1623, 1405], [1625, 1461], [659, 1496]]}, {"text": "drawing. White is usually best for drawings like", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[659, 1514], [1621, 1476], [1623, 1529], [661, 1566]]}, {"text": "this. Never choose a coloured sheet for a black", "conf": 0.933, "box": [[656, 1583], [1625, 1541], [1628, 1601], [658, 1642]]}, {"text": "and white work. Make sure that the picture is", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[655, 1652], [1627, 1609], [1630, 1676], [657, 1718]]}, {"text": "pasted right in the centre. You can also keep a", "conf": 0.928, "box": [[657, 1732], [1623, 1687], [1626, 1743], [659, 1789]]}, {"text": "slightly greater margin at the bottom.", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[660, 1801], [1431, 1778], [1433, 1831], [662, 1854]]}, {"text": "Fig: 5.2", "conf": 0.884, "box": [[314, 1965], [438, 1965], [438, 2007], [314, 2007]]}, {"text": "72", "conf": 0.666, "box": [[1491, 2003], [1557, 1997], [1563, 2052], [1497, 2059]]}, {"text": "ScannedwithCamScanner", "conf": 0.903, "box": [[1094, 2325], [1273, 2325], [1273, 2342], [1094, 2342]]}]}